    {
      "day": 26,
      "line": "They're named, every one: Deshawn Delgado, Dmitri Osei, Marcus Rossi. Your move — ask them questions (up to three), call a MOOT on it, or turn them away at the edge of the firelight."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "Travel 3 tiles to trail edge.\n— An old trail —\nThe trail is worn smooth as an old coin. Deer, probably. Probably."
    },
    {
      "day": 29,
      "line": "They waited three days at the edge of your fire. Nobody called the moot. Deshawn nods — not angry, just done — and they walk."
    },
    {
      "day": 49,
      "line": "Emberhold watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer. (Trust -8.)"
    },
