      "day": 82,
      "line": "Dounia spends the afternoon with the colonies of umbrella-like leaves, single lemon-sized fruit hidden underneath — look, smell, the smallest taste, then waiting. Edible, but it argues on the way down. The fire's verdict: food, carefully. Small amounts."
    },
    {
